# Project Architecture

This is an open-source esports broadcast overlay system.

## Stack

- Bun runtime and package manager
- Turborepo
- TypeScript
- React + Vite
- Hono backend
- shadcn/ui for dashboard UI
- Tailwind CSS
- Zod for validation
- Zustand for realtime client state
- TanStack Query for REST/API state
- SQLite + Drizzle when persistence is needed

Never introduce npm, pnpm or yarn commands. Use Bun.

## Monorepo

Apps:
- `apps/dashboard`: configuration and control UI
- `apps/overlay`: OBS browser-source overlay
- `apps/server`: local Hono server, GSI receiver and WebSocket server

Packages:
- `packages/gsi`: raw CS2 GSI schemas, parsing and Valve-specific logic
- `packages/game-state`: game-independent normalized state and events
- `packages/maps`: map metadata, world→radar transform, facing helpers
- `packages/theme`: shared theme types and tokens
- `packages/presentation`: player presentation config, portrait resolver, operator registry
- `packages/ui`: shared dashboard UI components
- `packages/database`: persistence
- `packages/config`: shared configuration

## Boundaries

Keep packages independent of applications.

`packages/game-state` MUST NOT depend on:
- React
- Hono
- database code
- CS2-specific GSI structures

Player presentation (portraits, display-name overrides) is configuration, not GameState.
It rides on `ServerMessage` as `{ type: "presentation" }` the same way theme does.

`packages/gsi` may depend on `game-state`, but `game-state` must never depend on `gsi`.

`packages/maps` must not depend on React, Hono, or `packages/gsi`. `packages/game-state` must not depend on `packages/maps` or radar artwork.

The overlay must never consume raw CS2 GSI payloads.

Correct flow:

CS2 GSI
→ GSI parser
→ normalized GameState
→ state engine
→ WebSocket
→ overlay

Map metadata and world→radar math live in `packages/maps`. Do not implement Valve overview formulas in React.

Do not bypass this architecture.

## UI

Business logic and GSI parsing must not live inside React components.

React components should primarily render already-normalized state.

Overlay components must not create their own WebSocket connections.
Use one centralized realtime store/client.